  "new_claims": [
    "primitive shell idempotents are orthogonal, complete, and classify all algebra idempotents by subsets of divisors",
    "primitive shells are recovered from widths by explicit M\u00f6bius inversion",
    "prime-power widths are the unique least separating canonical-width family",
    "every primitive shell is a Boolean product of prime-power width thresholds and complements",
    "prime-power canonical widths generate the full divisor-coordinate algebra via Algebra.adjoin",
    "any canonical-width family generating the full algebra contains every prime-power width",
    "number of prime-power generator thresholds equals Omega(T)",
    "primitive shells and canonical widths factor prime-by-prime through valuation selectors/thresholds",
    "divisor labels are canonically equivalent to bounded prime-valuation vectors",
    "divisor-coordinate algebra is algebra-equivalent to functions on the finite product of valuation chains",
    "complexity ledger: generator count Omega(T), algebra dimension product_p(v_p(T)+1), idempotent count 2^dimension"
  ],
  "explicit_boundaries": [
    "Bell generalized Cobham theorem remains an external input to the earlier two-radix collapse-to-cyclotomic step and is not formalized here",
    "the integral base-independent normal form remains false in the naive form; the square-sequence radix-prime obstruction is retained",
    "the package proves a product-coordinate algebra equivalence, not a separately constructed categorical tensor-product equivalence of local algebras"
  ],
